{"parentUuid":"21cd36aa-f846-45c3-8625-bec42d79ad3a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a2bbf0cd35f724a3c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CgL7WEzXf265RuqR17QZza","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools HiGHS solver wrapper integration Python LP relaxation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Solving an LP Problem | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/lp/lp_example\"},{\"title\":\"Google OR-Tools: ortools.math_opt.python.parameters.SolveParameters Class Reference\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/python/classortools_1_1math__opt_1_1python_1_1parameters_1_1SolveParameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - snkas/python-ortools-lp-parser: Fan-written linear program file (.lp) parser which returns an or-tools solver object. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/snkas/python-ortools-lp-parser\"},{\"title\":\"HiGHS optimization solver - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HiGHS_optimization_solver\"},{\"title\":\"HiGHS - High-performance parallel linear optimization software\",\"url\":\"https://highs.dev/\"},{\"title\":\"Google OR-Tools: ortools.linear_solver.pywraplp.Solver Class Reference\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/python/classortools_1_1linear__solver_1_1pywraplp_1_1Solver.html\"},{\"title\":\"List of options · HiGHS Documentation\",\"url\":\"https://ergo-code.github.io/HiGHS/dev/options/definitions/\"},{\"title\":\"Add support to the HiGHS solver MathOpt · Issue #3116 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3116\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.linear_solver.pywraplp API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/linear_solver/pywraplp.html\"},{\"title\":\"Get Started with OR-Tools for Python | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/introduction/python\"}]\n\nHere are the key findings from the web search results:\n\n## OR-Tools and Solver Wrappers\n\nOR-Tools provides a linear optimization solver that is a wrapper for several different libraries for linear and mixed-integer optimization, including third-party libraries.\n\n## HiGHS Solver\n\nHiGHS is open-source software to solve linear programming (LP), mixed-integer programming (MIP), and convex quadratic programming (QP) models, written in C++ and published under an MIT license, with programming interfaces to C, Python, Julia, Rust, R, JavaScript, Fortran, and C#.\n\n## Integration Status\n\nWhile HiGHS is a powerful solver, the search results show that OR-Tools includes HiGHS specific solve parameters, indicating some level of support. However, a GitHub issue from February 2022 indicates there were discussions about adding more complete HiGHS integration to OR-Tools.\n\n## LP Relaxation in OR-Tools\n\nThe search results show that OR-Tools supports various LP solvers and their usage, though they don't specifically detail LP relaxation functionality in relation to HiGHS wrapper integration. The platform supports solvers like GLOP, PDLP, and others for linear programming problems.\n\nFor more detailed information about LP relaxation specifically with HiGHS in Python, you may want to check the official HiGHS documentation or OR-Tools' MathOpt API documentation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"dc8b9552-b045-4c35-8145-5c882d0302e8","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:52:51.463Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"21cd36aa-f846-45c3-8625-bec42d79ad3a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"24b1c712-301d-47da-b182-5c4f0345079a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a2bbf0cd35f724a3c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EYkixaB6jDJLbzCMFXTc86","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Mosek Fusion Python LP large scale integration academic license cost\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Mosek - Academic Licenses\",\"url\":\"https://www.mosek.com/products/academic-licenses/\"},{\"title\":\"Mosek · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/Mosek/\"},{\"title\":\"3 License Agreement — MOSEK Fusion API for Python 8.1.0.83\",\"url\":\"https://docs.mosek.com/8.1/pythonfusion/license-agreement-info.html\"},{\"title\":\"Mosek - Buy MOSEK\",\"url\":\"https://www.mosek.com/buy/\"},{\"title\":\"3 License Agreement — MOSEK Fusion API for Python 10.2.17\",\"url\":\"https://docs.mosek.com/10.2/pythonfusion/license-agreement-info.html\"},{\"title\":\"10 Technical guidelines — MOSEK Fusion API for Python 11.1 ...\",\"url\":\"https://docs.mosek.com/latest/pythonfusion/guidelines-fusion.html\"},{\"title\":\"Mosek - Try MOSEK\",\"url\":\"https://www.mosek.com/try/\"},{\"title\":\"Mosek - Commercial Pricing\",\"url\":\"https://www.mosek.com/sales/commercial-pricing/\"},{\"title\":\"10 Technical guidelines — MOSEK Fusion API for Python 11.0 ...\",\"url\":\"https://docs.mosek.com/11.0/pythonfusion/guidelines-fusion.html\"},{\"title\":\"Mosek - Personal Academic License\",\"url\":\"https://www.mosek.com/license/request/personal-academic/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about MOSEK Fusion Python and academic licenses:\n\n## MOSEK Overview\nMOSEK is a large scale optimization software that solves Linear, Quadratic, Semidefinite and Mixed Integer problems.\n\n## Academic License Cost\nAcademic users are eligible for one of the free Academic Licenses. Additionally, free of charge trial licenses as well as licenses for non-commercial academic use can be obtained from https://www.mosek.com.\n\n## License Requirements\nMOSEK is a commercial product that always needs a valid license to work. However, for academic purposes, the licenses are provided at no cost.\n\nThe search results indicate that MOSEK offers free academic licenses for students and professors, though the exact details and application process would require visiting the MOSEK website directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"fd563e11-2f6b-4295-bf1e-c46f95e77c9d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:52:51.820Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"24b1c712-301d-47da-b182-5c4f0345079a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"fa41fc78-e2a3-4bd1-9432-3a26b7e8f706","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a2bbf0cd35f724a3c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015snMhvKCHcSsSCzmPRQUwy","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"NVIDIA cuOpt LP barrier 2025 2026 license commercial free\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - NVIDIA/cuopt: GPU accelerated decision optimization · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/NVIDIA/cuopt\"},{\"title\":\"cuOpt | Decision Optimization | NVIDIA\",\"url\":\"https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/ai-data-science/products/cuopt/\"},{\"title\":\"GPU-Accelerated Optimization with GAMS and NVIDIA cuOpt\",\"url\":\"https://www.gams.com/blog/2025/09/gpu-accelerated-optimization-with-gams-and-nvidia-cuopt/\"},{\"title\":\"NVIDIA Virtual GPU Software Packaging, Pricing, and Licensing Guide — NVIDIA Virtual GPU Software Packaging, Pricing, and Licensing Guide\",\"url\":\"https://docs.nvidia.com/vgpu/packaging-pricing-licensing-guide/latest/\"},{\"title\":\"Pricing — NVIDIA Enterprise Licensing Guide\",\"url\":\"https://docs.nvidia.com/ai-enterprise/planning-resource/licensing-guide/latest/pricing.html\"},{\"title\":\"Solve Linear Programs Using the GPU-Accelerated Barrier Method in NVIDIA cuOpt | NVIDIA Technical Blog\",\"url\":\"https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/solve-linear-programs-using-the-gpu-accelerated-barrier-method-in-nvidia-cuopt/\"},{\"title\":\"LP/QP Features — NVIDIA cuOpt (26.02)\",\"url\":\"https://docs.nvidia.com/cuopt/user-guide/latest/lp-qp-features.html\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction — NVIDIA cuOpt (26.04)\",\"url\":\"https://docs.nvidia.com/cuopt/user-guide/latest/introduction.html\"},{\"title\":\"NVIDIA cuOpt download | SourceForge.net\",\"url\":\"https://sourceforge.net/projects/nvidia-cuopt.mirror/\"},{\"title\":\"Licensing — NVIDIA Virtual GPU (vGPU): FAQ\",\"url\":\"https://docs.nvidia.com/vgpu/faq/latest/nls.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding NVIDIA cuOpt LP barrier and licensing:\n\n## Overview\nNVIDIA cuOpt is an open source, GPU-accelerated engine for decision optimization, excelling in mixed-integer programming (MIP), linear programming (LP), vehicle routing problems (VRPs), and quadratic programming (QP).\n\n## LP Barrier Method\nThe latest cuOpt release includes a new solver for linear programs that uses the barrier method, which complements the existing cuOpt LP solvers, enabling engineers, researchers, and developers to solve large-scale linear programs quickly and accurately. Internal benchmarks show cuOpt barrier delivering over 8x average speedup compared to a leading open source CPU solver and over 2x average speedup compared to a popular commercial CPU solver on a public test set of large linear programs.\n\n## Licensing Requirements\nFor licensing, a license for NVIDIA AI Enterprise or membership in the NVIDIA Developer Program is required. This indicates that while cuOpt is open source, there are licensing considerations for enterprise deployment.\n\nThe search results show recent updates from 2025-2026, with the latest GAMS/cuOpt integration update noted as of April 2026. However, the search results do not contain specific information about free commercial licensing policies for cuOpt in 2025-2026, so I cannot provide details on that aspect.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"eb2db933-131c-46ef-bec7-c2cac7bdac5b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:52:52.046Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fa41fc78-e2a3-4bd1-9432-3a26b7e8f706","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"fd2ab2aa-0ae9-472d-9d8f-1281bbf82159","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a2bbf0cd35f724a3c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011eVeA5zEa7wTBGwaWNRvAg","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"PDLP large LP placement assignment problem performance limitation primal infeasibility\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"LP and MILP Settings — NVIDIA cuOpt (25.12)\",\"url\":\"https://docs.nvidia.com/cuopt/user-guide/latest/lp-milp-settings.html\"},{\"title\":\"Scaling up linear programming with PDLP\",\"url\":\"https://research.google/blog/scaling-up-linear-programming-with-pdlp/\"},{\"title\":\"PDLP: A Practical First-Order Method for Large-Scale Linear Programming\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2501.07018\"},{\"title\":\"Computational Guarantees for Restarted PDHG for LP based on\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Manuscript-1.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"[BUG] PDLP algorithm unexpectedly stops after approximately 755_000 - 800_000 iterations · Issue #71 · NVIDIA/cuopt\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/NVIDIA/cuopt/issues/71\"},{\"title\":\"LP, QP, and MILP Settings — NVIDIA cuOpt (26.02)\",\"url\":\"https://docs.nvidia.com/cuopt/user-guide/26.02.00/lp-qp-milp-settings.html\"},{\"title\":\"PDLP (Primal-Dual Hybrid Gradient Enhanced for LP): A New FOM–based Linear Programming LP Solver that Significantly Scales Up Linear Programming LP Solving Capabilities - MarkTechPost\",\"url\":\"https://www.marktechpost.com/2024/09/24/pdlp-primal-dual-hybrid-gradient-enhanced-for-lp-a-new-fom-based-linear-programming-lp-solver-that-significantly-scales-up-linear-programming-lp-solving-capabilities/\"},{\"title\":\"Computational Guarantees for Restarted PDHG for LP based on “Limiting Error Ratios” and LP Sharpness\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2312.14774\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - google-research/FirstOrderLp.jl: Experimental first-order solvers for linear and quadratic programming. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google-research/FirstOrderLp.jl\"},{\"title\":\"First-Order Methods for Linear Programming Haihao Lu 1 Introduction\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2403.14535\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found several relevant sources about PDLP (Primal-Dual Hybrid Gradient enhanced for Linear Programming) and its performance characteristics on large LP problems:\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**About PDLP:**\nPDLP is a practical first-order method for linear programming designed to solve large-scale LP problems. It is based on the primal-dual hybrid gradient (PDHG) method applied to the minimax formulation of LP and incorporates several enhancements including diagonal preconditioning, presolving, adaptive step sizes, adaptive restarting, and feasibility polishing.\n\n**Performance on Large Problems:**\nPDLP was evaluated on a new collection of eleven large-scale LP problems with sizes ranging from 125 million to 6.3 billion nonzeros, and PDLP solves eight of these instances to optimality gaps of 1% (with primal and dual feasibility errors of less than 10^-8) within six days on a single machine.\n\n**Primal Infeasibility Detection:**\nPDLP demonstrates the value of feasibility polishing on the Mittelmann benchmark and reports the performance of PDLP in detecting infeasibility on a standard collection of primal infeasible problems. Additionally, PDLP can detect infeasibility with little additional overhead.\n\n**Performance Limitations:**\nIn real-world scenarios, LP problems may often be infeasible or unbounded. In response to this limitation, first-order methods (FOMs) have gained traction for large-scale LP problems.\n\nThe search results indicate that while PDLP is designed for large-scale problems, its performance on assignment problems specifically and challenges with very large placement problems would require more specialized literature.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c0ee2bc3-f087-4a9b-b697-179fc52ae6e6","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:52:52.894Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fd2ab2aa-0ae9-472d-9d8f-1281bbf82159","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e55693c1-5ba0-4854-bb3c-c7aa96f40445","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a2bbf0cd35f724a3c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017dDhYaHwBvcqBL1k89npNV","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Gurobi LP solver Python license academic 2026 size limit free\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"gurobipy · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/gurobipy/\"},{\"title\":\"Gurobi Academic License Program: Free Licenses for Academics | Gurobi - Gurobi Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.gurobi.com/academia/academic-program-and-licenses/\"},{\"title\":\"How do I obtain a free academic license? – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/articles/360040541251-How-do-I-obtain-a-free-academic-license\"},{\"title\":\"How do I resolve a \\\"Model too large for size-limited Gurobi license\\\" error? – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/articles/360051597492-How-do-I-resolve-a-Model-too-large-for-size-limited-Gurobi-license-error\"},{\"title\":\"Support for users with free trial licenses – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/articles/12249724751121-Support-for-users-with-free-trial-licenses\"},{\"title\":\"How do I get started with Gurobi for academic users? – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/articles/4534601245713-How-do-I-get-started-with-Gurobi-for-academic-users\"},{\"title\":\"Gurobi Solver Engine LP/MIP License | solver\",\"url\":\"https://www.solver.com/gurobi-solver-engine-lpmip-software\"},{\"title\":\"End User License Agreement Academic - Gurobi Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.gurobi.com/downloads/end-user-license-agreement-academic/\"},{\"title\":\"How do I obtain a Gurobi license? – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/articles/12684663118993-How-do-I-obtain-a-Gurobi-license\"},{\"title\":\"Academic Licence limitation – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/16095392796561-Academic-Licence-limitation\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about Gurobi LP solver Python licensing for academics:\n\n## Academic License\n\nAs a student or staff member of an academic institution, you qualify for a free, full product license. If you are a faculty member, student, or staff of a recognized degree-granting academic institution, you can obtain a free academic license from our website.\n\n## Size Limits\n\nA key advantage of Gurobi's academic license is that academic users receive the same full-featured, no-size limit version that commercial customers use. More specifically, academics get all the same Gurobi features and performance, with no limits on model size.\n\n## Free Trial/Evaluation Option\n\nIf you install Gurobi through pip or conda, it comes with a restricted license. This error typically occurs when Gurobi is installed using the pip or conda package distributors, which automatically include a size-limited license. However, you can get a free, full-featured license of the Gurobi Optimizer by formally registering for an academic license.\n\nThe search results indicate that academic licenses have no restrictions on problem size when properly obtained and activated, making them ideal for students and researchers at degree-granting institutions.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"d301029c-3c9b-45a0-85b4-1621b4506911","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:52:53.094Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e55693c1-5ba0-4854-bb3c-c7aa96f40445","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"8cf0b6d5-6f14-48c6-a578-38e08f07df40","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a2bbf0cd35f724a3c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GP8QXhi4FXx2mP2TaMr33E","type":"tool_result","content":"# LP Solvers Benchmarked (April 29, 2026)\n\n**Tested Solvers with Versions:**\n- CLP-1.17.7\n- COPT-8.0.0\n- MOSEK-11.1.11\n- HiGHS-1.14.0\n- ORTOOLS-9.5 (GLOP)\n- SOPLEX-8.0.0\n- XOPT-0.0.8\n\n**Performance Ranking** (by scaled geometric mean of runtimes):\n\n1. **COPT** – 1.0 (baseline)\n2. **XOPT** – 6.63\n3. **HiGHS** – 13.1\n4. **CLP** – 27.4\n5. **GLOP** – 59.7\n6. **MOSEK** – 104\n7. **SOPLEX** – 3,996\n\n**Success Rate** (problems solved):\nCOPT led with 65 of the test instances completed, while SOPLEX and CLP each solved 52 and 40 respectively. GLOP and MOSEK solved 53 and 52 cases, with XOPT successfully completing 52 instances.\n\nThe benchmark evaluated performance on finding optimal basic solutions across 65 test cases, with results shifted geometrically by 10 seconds."}]},"uuid":"7434af8a-f56c-49ca-a797-2e3406c67137","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:52:55.333Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8cf0b6d5-6f14-48c6-a578-38e08f07df40","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"31db9fac-96c6-4286-ac15-94525843b9ee","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a2bbf0cd35f724a3c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TECQzZ6in4hr7LyYVygxbA","type":"tool_result","content":"# LP Feasibility Solvers Benchmark (May 6, 2026)\n\n## Tested Solvers\n\n**CPU-based:**\n- COPT 8.0.0/3\n- MOSEK 11.1.11\n- HiGHS 1.14.0\n- KNITRO 15.0.0\n- ORTOOLS 9.10 (PDLP)\n- XOPT 0.0.8\n- HPR-LP-C 0.1.1\n\n**GPU-based:**\n- cuOpt 26.02\n- cuPDLPx 0.2.9\n\n## Performance Ranking (Scaled Geometric Mean)\n\n1. **COPTG** (CPU barrier) — 1.19\n2. **cuPDLPx** (GPU) — 1.82\n3. **COPT** (CPU) — 1.67\n4. **XOPT** (CPU) — 9.63\n5. **HiGHS** (CPU) — 17.2\n6. **KNITRO** (CPU) — 28.5\n7. **PDLP** (CPU) — 27.8\n8. **MOSEK** (CPU) — 4.93\n9. **HPR-LP-C** (CPU) — 2.60\n10. **cuOpt** (GPU concurrent) — 1.19\n\nThe benchmark ran on Linux with an i7-11700K processor and 64GB RAM for CPU tests; GPU tests used NVIDIA B200 hardware. COPTG achieved the lowest scaled runtime, while cuPDLPx ranked second among GPU solvers."}]},"uuid":"b0d598a3-3a71-4590-acf2-88e785f815fb","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:52:55.345Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"31db9fac-96c6-4286-ac15-94525843b9ee","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
