{"parentUuid":"7096fd91-28ff-499f-abe3-7e753623eff5","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a2bbf0cd35f724a3c","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01CrFcPBibSqU7UkXTj8xs4H","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Dgz9FWwTdtgcwEB1282jHT","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"or-tools\" HiGHS pywraplp.Solver.HIGHS_LINEAR_PROGRAMMING availability 2025"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7708,"cache_read_input_tokens":33582,"output_tokens":348,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7708},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":348,"cache_read_input_tokens":33582,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7708,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7708,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caox6e7QjjdcSvu2xWu6q","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"b8ff0bfe-9f36-49e6-8bc0-6968ad7622de","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:01.593Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b8ff0bfe-9f36-49e6-8bc0-6968ad7622de","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a2bbf0cd35f724a3c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dgz9FWwTdtgcwEB1282jHT","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"or-tools\" HiGHS pywraplp.Solver.HIGHS_LINEAR_PROGRAMMING availability 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Google OR-Tools: ortools.linear_solver.pywraplp.Solver Class Reference\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/python/classortools_1_1linear__solver_1_1pywraplp_1_1Solver.html\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.linear_solver.pywraplp API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/linear_solver/pywraplp.html\"},{\"title\":\"HiGHS - High-performance parallel linear optimization software\",\"url\":\"https://highs.dev/\"},{\"title\":\"Solving an LP Problem | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/lp/lp_example\"},{\"title\":\"4 Ways to Solve Linear Programming in Python | by Chong Jing Ting | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@chongjingting/4-ways-to-solve-linear-programming-in-python-b4af36b7894d\"},{\"title\":\"Solving a MIP Problem | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/mip/mip_example\"},{\"title\":\"Optimization Solvers (Part 2): Linear Programming with OR-Tools | by Train, Validate and Test | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@pauljohncronin/linear-programming-with-or-tools-e541a272c4a0\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/linear_solver/samples/linear_programming_example.py at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/linear_solver/samples/linear_programming_example.py\"},{\"title\":\"Software for solving linear programming problems\",\"url\":\"https://people.math.carleton.ca/~kcheung/math/notes/MATH5801/02/2_4_software.html\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction to Linear Programming in Python | TDS Archive\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/data-science/introduction-to-linear-programming-in-python-9261e7eb44b\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about OR-Tools and its solver options, but I didn't find specific information about `HIGHS_LINEAR_PROGRAMMING` in pywraplp.Solver. Let me search for more specific information about HiGHS integration with OR-Tools in 2025.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"HiGHS - High-performance parallel linear optimization software\",\"url\":\"https://highs.dev/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ERGO-Code/HiGHS: Linear optimization software · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ERGO-Code/HiGHS\"},{\"title\":\"HiGHS optimization solver - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HiGHS_optimization_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Best Open‑Source Linear Programming Solver\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/best-open-source-linear-programming-solver/best-open-source-linear-programming-solver-2395c1f9070e\"},{\"title\":\"About · HiGHS Documentation\",\"url\":\"https://ergo-code.github.io/HiGHS/stable/\"},{\"title\":\"HiGHS\",\"url\":\"https://www.gams.com/latest/docs/S_HIGHS.html\"},{\"title\":\"HiGHS | LinkedIn\",\"url\":\"https://uk.linkedin.com/company/highs-opt\"},{\"title\":\"Linear Programming, the HiGHS Optimization library and MATLAB » The MATLAB Blog - MATLAB & Simulink\",\"url\":\"https://blogs.mathworks.com/matlab/2024/11/04/linear-programming-the-highs-optimization-library-and-matlab/\"},{\"title\":\"HiGHS-js linear programming\",\"url\":\"https://lovasoa.github.io/highs-js/\"},{\"title\":\"Software | School of Mathematics | School of Mathematics\",\"url\":\"https://maths.ed.ac.uk/research/data-decisions/optimization-and-operational-research/software\"}]\n\nLet me search more specifically for OR-Tools HiGHS integration and whether HIGHS_LINEAR_PROGRAMMING is available.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Advanced LP Solving | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/lp/lp_advanced\"},{\"title\":\"Solving an LP Problem | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/lp/lp_example\"},{\"title\":\"GLOP - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GLOP\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/linear_solver/linear_solver.proto at main · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/main/ortools/linear_solver/linear_solver.proto\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/linear_solver/linear_solver.h at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/linear_solver/linear_solver.h\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - google/or-tools: Google's Operations Research tools: · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization\"},{\"title\":\"Scaling up linear programming with PDLP\",\"url\":\"https://research.google/blog/scaling-up-linear-programming-with-pdlp/\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OR-Tools\"},{\"title\":\"Linear Optimization | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/lp\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found definitive information about HiGHS support in OR-Tools. Here's what I discovered:\n\n## OR-Tools HiGHS Integration\n\nOR-Tools includes `HIGHS_LINEAR_PROGRAMMING` (enum value 15) as a supported solver type, and the library also supports `HIGHS_MIXED_INTEGER_PROGRAMMING` (enum value 16).\n\nHiGHS is callable from Google's OR-Tools, and this integration appears to be active and available. The solver can be used through the pywraplp interface by calling:\n\n```python\nsolver = pywraplp.Solver.CreateSolver(\"HIGHS_LP\")\n```\n\nor for mixed-integer problems:\n\n```python\nsolver = pywraplp.Solver.CreateSolver(\"HIGHS_MIP\")\n```\n\nThis integration leverages HiGHS's incorporation of PDLP (first-order LP solver) starting in version 1.7.0 in March 2024, which enhances the capabilities of the solver within OR-Tools.\n\nThe availability of HiGHS in OR-Tools continues into 2025 and beyond, as HiGHS provides the default LP and MIP solvers in MATLAB and the SciPy system, demonstrating widespread adoption and ongoing support across multiple platforms.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"04933a22-df52-4cc3-ad0f-76b1ec5e61e8","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:12.263Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b8ff0bfe-9f36-49e6-8bc0-6968ad7622de","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"04933a22-df52-4cc3-ad0f-76b1ec5e61e8","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a2bbf0cd35f724a3c","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01JCDHmTMLLMgdq4ufAVkFYf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"数据足够了，开始整理输出。\n\n---\n\n# 现代 Interior Point LP Solver 调研报告（2024-2026）\n\n## 一、横向对比表\n\n| Solver | 版本 | 类型 | License | 学术免费 | OR-Tools 集成 | LP 性能（Mittelmann scaled mean，越小越好） |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **COPT**（杉数） | 8.0 | 商业 IPM+Simplex | 商业付费（询价，类 Gurobi 量级） | 是，365 天续期 | 否（需手写桥接） | **1.0**（基线，第一名） |\n| **COPT-G**（GPU 版） | 8.0 | GPU barrier | 同上 | 同上 | 否 | **1.19**（feas benchmark 第一） |\n| **cuPDLPx** | 0.2.9 | GPU 一阶法 | MIT 开源 | 自由 | 否（独立 binary，需 H100/B200） | **1.82**（feas benchmark 第二），比 cuPDLP 快 2-5×，比 PDLP CPU 快 ~15× |\n| **NVIDIA cuOpt** barrier | 26.02 | GPU IPM+PDLP 并发 | 开源 + AI Enterprise | 注册 NVIDIA Dev 即可 | 否 | **1.19** concurrent（开源第一，整体第二） |\n| **Gurobi 12** | 12.x | 商业 IPM+Simplex | 商业 ~$10k+/座；学术全功能免费 | 是，无大小限制 | **官方支持**（pywraplp + MathOpt） | 已退出 Mittelmann（2024-08），历史第一档 |\n| **Mosek 11.1** | 11.1.11 | 商业纯 IPM（齐次自对偶） | 商业询价；学术免费 30 天可续 | 是 | 否（需手写） | **4.93** feas / **104** lpopt（在大稀疏 LP 上偏弱） |\n| **HiGHS 1.14** | 1.14.0（HiPO/IPX） | 开源 Simplex+IPM | MIT | 自由 | **官方支持**（`HIGHS_LP` enum 15） | **13.1** lpopt / **17.2** feas（开源最强） |\n| **PDLP**（OR-Tools 内置） | 9.10 | CPU 一阶法 | Apache 2.0 | 自由 | **原生**（GLOP/PDLP 一等公民） | **27.8** feas（中等，规模越大越赚） |\n| **GLOP** | 9.5 | CPU Simplex | Apache 2.0 | 自由 | 原生 | **59.7** lpopt（小问题够用，大问题慢） |\n| **Clarabel** | 0.10+ | Rust IPM（conic） | Apache 2.0 | 自由 | 否 | 未上 Mittelmann，主打 QP/SOCP/SDP |\n| **SCS 3.2.11** | 3.2.11 | 一阶 ADMM | MIT | 自由 | 否 | NETLIB 上比 OSQP 快 16×，但不是大规模 LP 的强项 |\n| **CPLEX 22.1.2** | 22.1.2 | 商业 IPM+Simplex | 商业；学术 Initiative 全功能免费 | 是，无大小限 | 旧 pywraplp 有，MathOpt 暂未列 | 最近未参与 Mittelmann；历史与 Gurobi 同档 |\n\n数据来源：Mittelmann LPopt 2026-04-29、LPfeas 2026-05-06；cuPDLPx arXiv 2507.14051；HiGHS 1.12 引入 HiPO IPM 直接因子 + 并行；OR-Tools MathOpt 后端列表（GLOP/PDLP/CP-SAT/SCIP/GLPK/Gurobi/HiGHS）。\n\n## 二、针对本项目（70×70 + 266 设施 placement LP 松弛）的判断\n\n规模估算：70×70 = 4900 格、266 设施、若每个候选 placement 约 10⁴ 量级，松弛后变量约 10⁵-10⁶、约束 10⁶ 量级（端口绑定 + 通量守恒）。这是中型稀疏 LP，远低于 PDLP 的 10⁸-10⁹ 甜点区间，但比 GLOP 单纯形舒服的规模要大。\n\n- 这种规模下 **CPU IPM 的性价比最高**，PDLP/cuPDLPx 的低精度终止（1e-4-1e-6）对 area 上界 oracle 来说精度不够，会污染 Benders 切的有效性。\n- HiGHS 1.14 的 HiPO 是直接因子化 IPM，开源、MIT、和 OR-Tools 已经原生集成，切换成本最低。\n- 商业 IPM（Gurobi/COPT/Mosek）若学术 license 可用，性能多一档（10-100×），但绑定到外部 license 服务器，CI/批量并行时容易掉链子。\n- GPU solver（cuPDLPx、cuOpt barrier）对我们的规模 overkill，且 H100/B200 不在本机 D 盘环境内，启动成本不划算。\n\n## 三、推荐：area 上界 oracle 接 HiGHS\n\n**首选：HiGHS 1.14 via OR-Tools `pywraplp.Solver.CreateSolver(\"HIGHS_LP\")`**\n- 工程量：几十行包装，已有 OR-Tools 依赖（项目里 ortools 9.15.6755）\n- License：MIT，零负担，符合 AI Safety Contract 中\"oracle 不写 checkpoint\"的隔离要求\n- 性能：开源最强，比 GLOP 快约 4×，比 PDLP CPU 快约 2×，IPM 模式对中型稀疏 LP 比 simplex 更稳\n- 退出时给出可重现的 dual bound，可直接作为 Benders master 的 area 上界\n\n**备选：PDLP（已经在 OR-Tools 里），用作 sanity-check second oracle**\n- 同一 LP 跑两遍取 max(dual bound)，免费 cross-check，不增加新依赖\n\n**不建议：**\n- Gurobi/COPT/Mosek：商业 license 引入外部依赖、CI 噪声，且本项目目前是单机 Phase 3B 调优，性能差距不到一个数量级时不值得换\n- cuPDLPx/cuOpt：GPU 路径属于未来 S-stage 大规模放大时再考虑，当前规模收益小于运维成本\n- Clarabel/SCS：偏 QP/SOCP/SDP，纯 LP 不是它们的主场\n\n**落地路径（一周内可完成）：**\n1. 升级 ortools 到带 HIGHS enum 的版本（≥9.7 都有），写一个 `src/oracles/highs_area_oracle.py`，输入 master LP relaxation、输出 dual bound + 求解时间\n2. 加 PDLP 第二 oracle 做 cross-check，二者 dual bound 不一致时打 WARN（这是 AI 安全契约里 UNKNOWN 分类器的天然输入）\n3. shadow 模式接进 outer_search，对比纯 CP-SAT 路径的 wall-time 缩减\n\nSources:\n- [cuPDLPx GitHub](https://github.com/MIT-Lu-Lab/cuPDLPx)\n- [cuPDLPx arXiv 2507.14051](https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.14051)\n- [Mittelmann LPopt benchmark](https://plato.asu.edu/ftp/lpopt.html)\n- [Mittelmann LPfeas benchmark](https://plato.asu.edu/ftp/lpfeas.html)\n- [Gurobi withdraws from Mittelmann (Aug 2024)](https://www.gurobi.com/resources/update-on-gurobi-participation-in-mittelmann-benchmarks/)\n- [HiGHS 1.12 HiPO IPM newsletter](https://highs.dev/assets/HiGHS_Newsletter_25_0.pdf)\n- [HiGHS docs solvers](https://ergo-code.github.io/HiGHS/dev/solvers/)\n- [OR-Tools MathOpt overview](https://developers.google.com/optimization/math_opt)\n- [NVIDIA cuOpt LP barrier blog](https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/solve-linear-programs-using-the-gpu-accelerated-barrier-method-in-nvidia-cuopt/)\n- [Clarabel.rs GitHub](https://github.com/oxfordcontrol/Clarabel.rs)\n- [SCS docs](https://www.cvxgrp.org/scs/)\n- [Mosek 11 academic license](https://www.mosek.com/products/academic-licenses/)\n- [Gurobi academic program](https://www.gurobi.com/academia/academic-program-and-licenses/)\n- [CPLEX academic initiative](https://www.ibm.com/support/pages/ibm-ilog-optimization-academic-initiative)\n- [PDLP scaling blog (Google Research)](https://research.google/blog/scaling-up-linear-programming-with-pdlp/)\n- [COPT vs HiGHS benchmark commentary](https://github.com/ERGO-Code/HiGHS/discussions/1683)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2923,"cache_read_input_tokens":41290,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2923,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caox7tGjQDKbzyUSGJH5s","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"378ed038-1af8-423b-be64-602fff1992ef","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:54:10.680Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
